  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "Correctness",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The agent fixed all three abort paths with guards scoped to each command: an if-wrapped capture with rc for assert_slug, `|| true` on the grep pipeline in assert_line, and if-guarded slugify and cmp in assert_golden, so each failure becomes one FAIL, the run continues and the exit is still non-zero; the one small risk is that `2>&1` in assert_slug would mix stderr into the compared output on a successful run."
      },
      {
        "name": "Restraint",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "Only test/run-tests.sh changed, the agent restored slugify.sh after its crash simulation, and the tests, their names, the PASS/FAIL/Results format and the non-zero exit are all kept; the stderr merge in assert_slug is a small behaviour change nobody asked for."
      },
      {
        "name": "Explanation",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "The reply names the exact mechanism: under set -euo pipefail, a command substitution that exits non-zero on the very result the helper should report (grep finds no match, cmp sees a difference, slugify crashes) kills the runner, hiding the Results line and every later test; it also says plainly that the grep-miss and cmp-difference paths were not tested."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 9.0
  },
